---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import {url} from '../../../data/plugins';
import {loopClub as p} from '../../../data/loop-club';
---
<Base title="Loop Club — 16-track looper for MPC Sample | Kim’s Work" description={p.summary}>
<article class="wrap guide">
<a class="back" href={url('software/sample-mods/')}>← MPC Sample mods</a>
<p class="eyebrow">MPC SAMPLE · PUBLIC PREVIEW {p.version} · BY KIM</p>
<h1>Build a loop.<br/>Keep playing.</h1>
<p class="lead">Sixteen independent audio, synth and drum tracks. Record a phrase, finish at a bar and keep it looping while you build the next layer.</p>
<figure class="device-shot"><img src={url(`images/${p.image}`)} width="320" height="240" alt={p.imageAlt}/><figcaption>Actual MPC Sample screen · Native 320×240 display.</figcaption></figure>
<div class="manual-actions"><a class="button" href={p.download}>Download preview {p.version}</a><a href={url('mods/loop-club/manual/')}>Read the manual →</a><a href={p.release}>Release & SHA-256 ↗</a></div>
<p class="platform-note">MPC Sample firmware 1.3.0.12 only. An SD preload mod, not an MPC OS plugin or a firmware image. Preserve your existing autorun before installing.</p>
<h2>The looper comes first.</h2>
<p>Choose Audio / Synth / Drum. SHIFT+track pad starts recording; SHIFT+the same pad finishes at the next bar. The LOOP screen stays visible and ordinary pads play the selected source. REPLACE sets a new length; OVERDUB retains the old length. Each track keeps its own length: a one-bar part repeats alongside a four-bar phrase. DATA selects tracks; the fader follows with pickup. SHIFT+LOOP opens COPY / DELETE / MOVE; Undo/Redo protects the latest edit.</p>
<div class="feature-grid"><section><h3>Synth and stereo movement</h3><p>Two oscillators, individual Tune/Fine/Level, resonant filter and separate amp/filter ADSRs. A six-shape tempo-sync LFO moves Pitch and Filter. Tremolo, Auto Pan and Auto Filter are independent insert effects; legacy modulation values remain editable.</p></section><section><h3>Drums with room to shape</h3><p>Sixteen original procedural sounds, musical pattern generation and subdivision velocity accents. Two layers per sound with Volume, Tune, relative Shift, Decay and sample REV. Optional user banks stay outside the app. Import a Drum XPM by choosing its A–H bank; retain up to four original velocity/cycle/random zones under Layer1.</p></section><section><h3>Tap an effect. Keep the others.</h3><p>Track and master FX use 4×4 pad boards with momentary press/release and SHIFT-latched states. Two track effects stay on together without silent replacement. Master combines Dust, Drive, Squeeze, Wobble, Dub Echo, Duck and two custom FX; bypass keeps settings.</p></section><section><h3>Sidechain that follows your beat</h3><p>Use an individual drum or a whole track as the detector. Duck the other tracks, choose a custom target mask, or pump the full master. Depth, sensitivity, free/tempo-synced recovery and a reduction meter.</p></section></div>
<div class="screens-grid">{[['edit','Copy, delete and move loops without leaving the workspace'],['fx','Press a master effect pad to show its controls immediately'],['synth','Two oscillators and independent amp/filter envelopes']].map(([name,alt])=><figure><img src={url(`images/loop-club-${name}-0.9.3.webp`)} width="320" height="240" alt={alt} loading="lazy"/><figcaption>{alt}. Actual MPC Sample capture.</figcaption></figure>)}</div>
<h2>Hear it. Then play the effects.</h2>
<p>A short piece built on the MPC Sample, followed by live filter sweeps, repeat punches, reverse, drive/crush and tape-stop drops. This is actual device screen capture and USB output, triggered through remote controls. Song-building footage is from0.9.0; the updated FX section shows0.9.3 with direct parameter controls below the pads.</p>
<video controls playsinline preload="none" poster={url('images/loop-club-performance-0.9.3.webp')} aria-label="Loop Club actual MPC Sample effects performance"><source src={p.performanceVideo} type="video/mp4"/>Your browser can download the performance below.</video>
<div class="manual-actions"><a href={p.performanceVideo}>Download FX performance (46 seconds)</a><a href={p.fullVideo}>Watch or download the full song-building video (2:12)</a></div>
<p class="platform-note">The demo uses the owner’s optional Cosmic Vintage drum bank. The download includes original procedural drums only; that commercial bank and its source samples are not distributed.</p>
<h2>New in this update.</h2><p>Audio INPUT / CHROMATIC / CHOP recording, Warp, complete MIDI releases, clip Undo/Redo, XPM bank import, in-place loop edits and bar-end recording handoff. Format7 saves retain each loop’s relative alignment; formats1–6 still open.</p>
<h2>What this preview verifies.</h2>
<p>293 Debug and 293 Release tests, strict host/ARM64 Clippy and ARM64 builds pass. Actual remote-control checks cover navigation, synth editing, loop recording, count-in, drum generation, audio-frame capture, chopping, mixers, simultaneous FX and save/recall. Named-device USB recordings verify stereo movement and drum-triggered ducking. The screenshots above come from the active device display.</p>
<p>Physical finger controls, calibrated analog latency, final power-cycle recovery and long-session reliability remain separate acceptance checks.32 voices are shared; CPU headroom depends on polyphony and FX. A short stress run is not a guarantee for every project.</p>
<h2>Know the boundaries.</h2>
<ul><li>USB currently exposes one stereo pair. MAIN / USB / MAIN+USB destinations do not provide individual drum USB stems.</li><li>USB-input recording, chromatic/chop MIDI capture and bounded Warp are included. XPM native inserts/envelopes/Warp and bank MIDI pattern import are not reproduced. GRID displays the first 64 events.</li><li>The download contains no commercial samples, personal expansions, firmware or QA management agent.</li><li>Source and SDK licenses are MIT. Follow the <a href={url('mods/loop-club/manual/')}>installation and recovery instructions</a> before changing your SD boot.</li></ul>
</article>
</Base>
